# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, we demonstrate how to leverage advanced error-mitigation tools in Qiskit to improve expectation value estimation in noisy quantum experiments.\n"
msgstr "Sa tutorial na ito, ipinapakita natin kung paano gamitin ang mga advanced na error-mitigation tools sa Qiskit upang mapabuti ang expectation value estimation sa noisy quantum experiments.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is propagated noise absorption (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"
msgstr "What is propagated noise absorption (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Propagated noise absorption is a technique for mitigating gate errors by propagating the observable through the inverse noise channel affecting two-qubit gates, resulting in a noise-mitigating observable.*\n"
msgstr "*Ang propagated noise absorption ay isang teknik para pagaanin ang gate errors sa pamamagitan ng pag-propagate ng observable sa pamamagitan ng inverse noise channel na nakaaapekto sa two-qubit gates, na nagreresulta sa isang noise-mitigating observable.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can use quantum error mitigation to extract useful expectation values from noisy quantum hardware without requiring full fault tolerance. PNA specifically focuses on absorbing noise effects into the observable itself rather than modifying the circuit operations.\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating gamitin ang quantum error mitigation upang kumuha ng kapaki-pakinabang na expectation values mula sa noisy quantum hardware nang hindi kinakailangan ng full fault tolerance. Ang PNA ay partikular na nakatuon sa pag-absorb ng mga epekto ng noise sa observable mismo sa halip na baguhin ang mga circuit operations.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each noisy gate in a quantum circuit can be modeled as an ideal gate followed by a noise channel. PNA learns or characterizes these noise channels and defines their inverses. Instead of inserting the inverse operations into the hardware execution (which is typically infeasible), PNA propagates the inverse noise channels forward through the circuit and applies them to the observable. This process transforms the observable $O$ into a new operator $\\tilde{O}$, such that measuring $\\tilde{O}$ on the noisy circuit yields the same expectation value as measuring $O$ on an ideal, noise-free circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat noisy gate sa isang quantum circuit ay maaaring i-model bilang isang ideal gate na sinusundan ng isang noise channel. Natututo o kina-characterize ng PNA ang mga noise channel na ito at tinutukoy ang kanilang mga inverse. Sa halip na iturok ang inverse operations sa hardware execution (na karaniwang hindi feasible), pina-propagate ng PNA ang inverse noise channels pasulong sa buong circuit at inilalapat ang mga ito sa observable. Ang prosesong ito ay nagbabago sa observable $O$ patungo sa isang bagong operator $\\tilde{O}$, kung saan ang pagsukat sa $\\tilde{O}$ sa noisy circuit ay nagbibigay ng parehong expectation value gaya ng pagsukat sa $O$ sa isang ideal, noise-free circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be summarized as:\n"
"1. Model each noisy gate $u_i$ as an ideal operation followed by a noise channel $\\Lambda_i$.\n"
"2. Learn or estimate each $\\Lambda_i$ using noise characterization tools.\n"
"3. Define and propagate the inverse noise maps $\\Lambda_i^{-1}$ forward through the circuit using Pauli transfer techniques.\n"
"4. Absorb these inverses into the observable, resulting in a noise-mitigated operator $\\tilde{O}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari itong ibuod bilang:\n"
"1. I-model ang bawat noisy gate $u_i$ bilang isang ideal operation na sinusundan ng isang noise channel $\\Lambda_i$.\n"
"2. Alamin o tantiyahin ang bawat $\\Lambda_i$ gamit ang mga noise characterization tools.\n"
"3. Tukuyin at i-propagate ang inverse noise maps $\\Lambda_i^{-1}$ pasulong sa buong circuit gamit ang Pauli transfer techniques.\n"
"4. I-absorb ang mga inverse na ito sa observable, na nagreresulta sa isang noise-mitigated operator $\\tilde{O}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the noise is described as a Pauli channel (or more generally as a sparse Pauli-Lindblad channel), this propagation can be performed efficiently using Pauli propagation. Pauli propagation provides a framework for approximating how inverse noise channels transform as they pass through layers of Clifford and non-Clifford operations, while controlling the computational complexity.\n"
msgstr "Kapag inilarawan ang noise bilang isang Pauli channel (o mas pangkalahatan bilang isang sparse Pauli-Lindblad channel), ang propagation na ito ay maisasagawa nang episyente gamit ang Pauli propagation. Nagbibigay ang Pauli propagation ng isang framework para sa pag-approximate kung paano nagbabago ang inverse noise channels habang dumaraan sila sa mga layer ng Clifford at non-Clifford operations, habang kinokontrol ang computational complexity.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By shifting the mitigation into the observable, PNA avoids the large sampling overhead that would otherwise come from inserting physical correction operations into the circuit. Instead, the original noisy circuit is executed, while the observable is transformed into a new operator $\\tilde{O}$ whose expectation value cancels the effects of noise.\n"
msgstr "Sa pamamagitan ng paglipat ng mitigation sa observable, iniiwasan ng PNA ang malaking sampling overhead na kung hindi man ay manggagaling sa pagtutok ng physical correction operations sa circuit. Sa halip, ang orihinal na noisy circuit ang isasagawa, habang ang observable ay binabago patungo sa isang bagong operator $\\tilde{O}$ na ang expectation value ay kumakansela sa mga epekto ng noise.\n"

