#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Setup {#setup}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PNA mitigates the *physical* two-qubit gate noise of a specific quantum processor. The workflow depends on two hardware services that have no meaningful analog on an ideal simulator:\n"
msgstr "Pinapagaan ng PNA ang *pisikal* na two-qubit gate noise ng isang partikular na quantum processor. Ang workflow ay umaasa sa dalawang hardware service na walang makabuluhang katumbas sa isang ideal na simulator:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NoiseLearnerV3` experimentally characterizes the sparse Pauli-Lindblad noise channel attached to each unique two-qubit layer of the transpiled circuit. On a noiseless simulator there is no noise to learn, and the propagated inverse channel would be the identity.\n"
msgstr "Eksperimental na kinakarakter ng `NoiseLearnerV3` ang sparse Pauli-Lindblad noise channel na nakadikit sa bawat natatanging two-qubit layer ng transpiled circuit. Sa isang noiseless na simulator, walang noise na matututunan, at ang propagated inverse channel ay magiging identity.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Executor` primitive samples the twirled, randomized circuits generated by `samplomatic` on a backend.\n"
msgstr "Sinasampol ng `Executor` primitive ang mga twirled, randomized na circuit na binuo ng `samplomatic` sa isang backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In principle you could substitute a synthetic noise model. For example, you could attach `PauliLindbladError` instructions with [Qiskit Aer](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-aer) and pass the resulting noisy circuit directly to `generate_noise_mitigating_observable`. However, this only validates the classical bookkeeping against noise you injected yourself, and obscures the point of the technique. For that reason we skip the simulator example and demonstrate the full PNA workflow directly on hardware, with each step of the Qiskit pattern broken out below.\n"
msgstr "Sa prinsipyo, maaari kang gumamit ng isang synthetic noise model bilang kapalit. Halimbawa, maaari kang mag-attach ng `PauliLindbladError` instructions gamit ang [Qiskit Aer](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-aer) at ipasa ang resultang noisy na circuit nang direkta sa `generate_noise_mitigating_observable`. Gayunpaman, ito ay bumabalido lamang sa classical bookkeeping laban sa noise na ikaw mismo ang nag-inject, at ito ay nagtatakip sa layunin ng teknik. Dahil dito, hindi natin isasagawa ang simulator example at direktang ipapakita ang buong PNA workflow sa hardware, na may bawat hakbang ng Qiskit pattern na inilalarawan sa ibaba.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now run the complete PNA workflow on a 30-site kicked Ising model executed on IBM Quantum&reg; hardware, following the four steps of a Qiskit pattern.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay isasagawa natin ang kumpletong PNA workflow sa isang 30-site na kicked Ising model na isinasagawa sa IBM Quantum&reg; hardware, sinusunod ang apat na hakbang ng Qiskit pattern.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: Map to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Generate the mirrored Trotter circuit and observable**\n"
msgstr "**Generate the mirrored Trotter circuit and observable**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this experiment, we will study the time dynamics of a 30-site kicked Ising model on a 1D spin chain. The Hamiltonian considered is:\n"
msgstr "Para sa eksperimentong ito, pag-aaralan natin ang time dynamics ng isang 30-site na kicked Ising model sa isang 1D spin chain. Ang Hamiltonian na isinasaalang-alang ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$,\n"
msgstr "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $J>0$ describes the coupling of nearest-neighbor spins, $i<j$, and the global transverse field, $h$, is set to $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. The further $h$ is from a Clifford angle (that is, $\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$), the more difficult it becomes to propagate the anti-noise generators through the circuit.\n"
msgstr "kung saan inilalarawan ng $J>0$ ang coupling ng nearest-neighbor spins, $i<j$, at ang global transverse field, $h$, ay itinakda sa $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. Kung mas malayo ang $h$ mula sa isang Clifford angle (ibig sabihin, $\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$), mas mahirap na i-propagate ang mga anti-noise generator sa circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the choice of observable, we will consider the average single-site magnetization, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, where $N$ is the number of sites.\n"
msgstr "Para sa pagpili ng observable, isasaalang-alang natin ang average single-site magnetization, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, kung saan ang $N$ ay ang bilang ng mga site.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/extracted-outputs/8fcb5af8-64f0-498a-821f-11bcd7aea203-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/extracted-outputs/8fcb5af8-64f0-498a-821f-11bcd7aea203-0.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem for hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: Optimize the problem for hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next step is to prepare our mirrored Trotter circuit for execution on real IBM Quantum hardware. Running on a QPU requires more than just constructing the abstract circuit, as we need to optimize it so that:\n"
msgstr "Ang susunod na hakbang ay ihanda ang ating mirrored Trotter circuit para sa pagpapatakbo sa tunay na IBM Quantum hardware. Ang pagpapatakbo sa isang QPU ay nangangailangan ng higit pa sa pagbuo lamang ng abstract circuit, dahil kailangan nating i-optimize ito upang:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**It respects the backend's native gate set and connectivity.**\n"
"Transpilation maps the logical circuit into an ISA circuit supported by the target backend. This ensures every gate and qubit interaction is physically realizable.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sumusunod ito sa native gate set at connectivity ng backend.**\n"
"Ina-map ng transpilation ang logical circuit patungo sa isang ISA circuit na sinusuportahan ng target backend. Tinitiyak nito na ang bawat gate at qubit interaction ay pisikal na maisasakatuparan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**We can characterize the noise at the level of circuit layers.**\n"
"PNA relies on learning and propagating inverse noise channels. To do this efficiently, we break the transpiled circuit into unique two-qubit \"boxed\" layers. These boxes allow us to associate each layer of the circuit with its own learned noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Makakarakter natin ang noise sa antas ng circuit layers.**\n"
"Umaasa ang PNA sa pagtuto at pag-propagate ng inverse noise channels. Upang gawin ito nang episyente, hinahati natin ang transpiled circuit sa mga natatanging two-qubit na \"boxed\" layer. Ang mga box na ito ay nagbibigay-daan sa atin na iugnay ang bawat layer ng circuit sa sarili nitong natutunang noise model.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**We can feed realistic noise models into PNA.**\n"
"Once the circuit has been boxed, we use the `NoiseLearnerV3` service to experimentally learn the Pauli noise channels affecting each unique two-qubit layer. These learned models are then linked back to the circuit through Samplomatic's annotations.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Makakapagpakain tayo ng makatotohanang noise model sa PNA.**\n"
"Sa sandaling na-box na ang circuit, ginagamit natin ang serbisyong `NoiseLearnerV3` upang eksperimental na matutunan ang mga Pauli noise channel na nakakaapekto sa bawat natatanging two-qubit layer. Ang mga natutunang modelong ito ay pagkatapos ay ikinokonekta pabalik sa circuit sa pamamagitan ng mga annotation ng Samplomatic.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Altogether, this step bridges the gap between an idealized mirrored circuit and a hardware-ready circuit with learned noise models. With this setup, PNA can propagate inverse noise channels through the circuit and adjust the observable accordingly.\n"
msgstr "Sa kabuuan, ang hakbang na ito ay nagbabahagi ng agwat sa pagitan ng isang idealized mirrored circuit at isang hardware-ready circuit na may natutunang mga noise model. Sa setup na ito, maaaring i-propagate ng PNA ang inverse noise channels sa buong circuit at i-adjust ang observable ayon dito.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connect to the backend and transpile to an ISA circuit {#connect-to-the-backend-and-transpile-to-an-isa-circuit}"
msgstr "Connect to the backend and transpile to an ISA circuit {#connect-to-the-backend-and-transpile-to-an-isa-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We first initialize IBM Quantum Compute Service and select a backend. Authenticate with your own account by following the [instructions to save your credentials](/guides/cloud-setup), after which `QiskitRuntimeService()` will pick them up automatically.\n"
msgstr "Una nating i-initialize ang IBM Quantum Compute Service at pumili ng backend. Mag-authenticate gamit ang sarili mong account sa pamamagitan ng pagsunod sa [instructions to save your credentials](/guides/cloud-setup), pagkatapos nito awtomatikong makukuha ito ng `QiskitRuntimeService()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we choose a connected chain of qubits on the backend and transpile the circuit onto it.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, pipili tayo ng isang connected chain ng mga qubit sa backend at i-transpile ang circuit dito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the `find_qubit_chain` helper defined in the Setup section, we select a line of `num_qubits` connected physical qubits. We then transpile with `optimization_level=0` and pin this chain as the `initial_layout`, which preserves the two-qubit-gate layer structure of the mirrored circuit exactly. That structure is what the boxing and noise-learning steps rely on, so a higher optimization level (which would cancel the mirrored gates) must be avoided here.\n"
msgstr "Gamit ang `find_qubit_chain` helper na tinukoy sa Setup section, pinipili natin ang isang linya ng `num_qubits` na konektadong pisikal na qubit. Pagkatapos ay nagtra-transpile tayo gamit ang `optimization_level=0` at ipinipin ang chain na ito bilang `initial_layout`, na eksaktong pinapanatili ang two-qubit-gate layer structure ng mirrored circuit. Ang structure na iyon ang inaasahan ng boxing at noise-learning steps, kaya dapat iwasan dito ang mas mataas na optimization level (na magkakansela sa mirrored gates).\n"

