# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise using `NoiseLearnerV3` {#learn-the-noise-using-noiselearnerv3}"
msgstr "Learn the noise using `NoiseLearnerV3` {#learn-the-noise-using-noiselearnerv3}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before we can apply PNA for error mitigation, we first need to characterize the noise acting on each unique two-qubit layer and the measurement layer in our circuit. To do this, we use the `NoiseLearnerV3` program to experimentally learn noise models for each layer identified earlier. The learner performs benchmarking-style experiments that estimate the noise channel affecting each layer and returns a result object containing the learned model.\n"
msgstr "Bago natin ilapat ang PNA para sa error mitigation, kailangan muna nating ikarakter ang noise na kumikilos sa bawat natatanging two-qubit layer at ang measurement layer sa ating circuit. Upang gawin ito, ginagamit natin ang `NoiseLearnerV3` program upang eksperimental na matutunan ang mga noise model para sa bawat layer na natukoy na kanina. Ang learner ay nagsasagawa ng mga eksperimentong tulad ng benchmarking na nagtataya sa noise channel na nakakaapekto sa bawat layer at nagbabalik ng result object na naglalaman ng natutunang modelo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We begin by identifying the unique layers in our circuit using `find_unique_box_instructions` from `samplomatic`. This ensures that we only learn the noise once per distinct layer type, minimizing the number of experiments and total shot cost. The resulting list of layers is passed to the noise learner.\n"
msgstr "Magsisimula tayo sa pagtukoy ng mga natatanging layer sa ating circuit gamit ang `find_unique_box_instructions` mula sa `samplomatic`. Tinitiyak nito na iisang beses lamang natin matututunan ang noise para sa bawat natatanging uri ng layer, na binabawasan ang bilang ng mga eksperimento at kabuuang gastos sa shot. Ang resultang listahan ng mga layer ay ipinapasa sa noise learner.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are a few key parameters that control how the noise is learned:\n"
msgstr "Mayroong ilang mahalagang parameter na kumokontrol kung paano matututunan ang noise:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_randomizations`: Number of random circuits used per learning configuration.\n"
msgstr "`num_randomizations`: Bilang ng random circuit na ginagamit sa bawat learning configuration.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`shots_per_randomization`: Number of shots taken per random learning circuit.\n"
msgstr "`shots_per_randomization`: Bilang ng shot na kinukuha sa bawat random learning circuit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`layer_pair_depths`: The circuit depths (measured in number of pairs) to use in learning experiments.\n"
msgstr "`layer_pair_depths`: Ang circuit depths (sinusukat sa bilang ng pairs) na gagamitin sa mga learning experiment.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`post_selection`: Enables edge-based post-selection using `rx` gates to apply post-measurement pulses.\n"
msgstr "`post_selection`: Nagbibigay-daan sa edge-based post-selection gamit ang mga `rx` gate upang ilapat ang post-measurement pulses.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the learned noise rates {#visualize-the-learned-noise-rates}"
msgstr "Visualize the learned noise rates {#visualize-the-learned-noise-rates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After learning the noise models, we can inspect the distribution of the inferred error rates for both one-qubit and two-qubit operations. The code below extracts the Pauli-Lindblad representations from the learned noise results and collects the corresponding noise rates.\n"
msgstr "Matapos matutunan ang mga noise model, maaari nating suriin ang distribution ng mga natutunang error rate para sa parehong one-qubit at two-qubit operations. Ang code sa ibaba ay kumukuha ng mga Pauli-Lindblad representation mula sa natutunang noise results at kinokolekta ang kaukulang mga noise rate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each learned layer:\n"
"- We convert the noise model to a sparse list of `(pstr, qubits, rate)` tuples, where `pstr` is the Pauli string acting on the given qubits and `rate` is the associated error rate.\n"
"- We separate the rates into one-qubit (`len(pstr) == 1`) and two-qubit (`len(pstr) == 2`) terms.\n"
"- The lists of rates are then sorted, and their median values are computed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa bawat natutunang layer:\n"
"- Kina-convert natin ang noise model sa isang sparse na listahan ng `(pstr, qubits, rate)` tuples, kung saan ang `pstr` ay ang Pauli string na kumikilos sa ibinigay na mga qubit at ang `rate` ay ang kaugnay na error rate.\n"
"- Hinahati natin ang mga rate sa one-qubit (`len(pstr) == 1`) at two-qubit (`len(pstr) == 2`) na mga termino.\n"
"- Ang mga listahan ng rate ay pinagsu-sort, at kinakalkula ang kanilang median values.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We plot the one-qubit (red) and two-qubit (blue) noise-rate distributions on a logarithmic scale, with their median values marked by vertical lines, so that we can compare the relative magnitudes of the learned Pauli-Lindblad generators. The ordering of the one- and two-qubit rates depends on the device and on the specific layers being characterized; in this run, the single-qubit (weight-1) generators carry the larger median rate.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita natin sa graph ang distribution ng one-qubit (pula) at two-qubit (asul) na noise rate sa logarithmic scale, na may kanilang median values na minarkahan ng vertical lines, upang maihambing natin ang relative magnitude ng natutunang Pauli-Lindblad generators. Ang pagkakasunud-sunod ng one- at two-qubit rates ay depende sa device at sa mga tiyak na layer na kinakarakter; sa run na ito, ang single-qubit (weight-1) na mga generator ang may mas malaking median rate.\n"

