# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Associate circuit boxes with learned noise {#associate-circuit-boxes-with-learned-noise}"
msgstr "Associate circuit boxes with learned noise {#associate-circuit-boxes-with-learned-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we have obtained noise models for each unique two-qubit layer, we need to link them to the corresponding `InjectNoise` annotations within the boxed circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nakuha na natin ang mga noise model para sa bawat natatanging two-qubit layer, kailangan nating ikonekta ang mga ito sa kaukulang mga `InjectNoise` annotation sa loob ng boxed circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `InjectNoise` directive is a `samplomatic` annotation that uses the single-qubit dressers to inject noise into the circuit in a controlled and configurable way. It enables modular noise modeling across different layers.\n"
msgstr "Ang `InjectNoise` directive ay isang `samplomatic` annotation na gumagamit ng single-qubit dressers upang mag-inject ng noise sa circuit sa isang kontrolado at configurable na paraan. Nagbibigay-daan ito sa modular noise modeling sa iba't ibang layer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each `InjectNoise` annotation includes:\n"
"- `InjectNoise.ref` - a unique identifier for the annotation. This is used by the `samplex` object to correctly assign the corresponding noise model.\n"
"- `InjectNoise.modifier_ref` *(optional)* - a secondary reference that allows scaling the assigned noise model by a multiplicative factor.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kasama sa bawat `InjectNoise` annotation:\n"
"- `InjectNoise.ref` - isang natatanging identifier para sa annotation. Ginagamit ito ng `samplex` object upang tama itong maitalaga sa kaukulang noise model.\n"
"- `InjectNoise.modifier_ref` *(opsyonal)* - isang pangalawang reference na nagbibigay-daan sa pag-scale ng itinalagang noise model gamit ang isang multiplicative factor.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this step, we build a mapping from each `InjectNoise.ref` to its corresponding learned noise model (`PauliLindbladMap`). This mapping ensures that each entangling gate layer in the circuit is paired with the appropriate noise model, so that noise effects are accurately applied during sampling and subsequent noise-mitigation steps.\n"
msgstr "Sa hakbang na ito, bumubuo tayo ng isang mapping mula sa bawat `InjectNoise.ref` patungo sa kaukulang natutunang noise model (`PauliLindbladMap`). Tinitiyak ng mapping na ito na ang bawat entangling gate layer sa circuit ay ipinares sa naaangkop na noise model, upang tumpak na mailapat ang mga epekto ng noise sa panahon ng sampling at kasunod na mga hakbang sa noise mitigation.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagate the observable through the learned anti-noise {#propagate-the-observable-through-the-learned-anti-noise}"
msgstr "Propagate the observable through the learned anti-noise {#propagate-the-observable-through-the-learned-anti-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As discussed above, this is done in two steps. First, we propagate an anti-noise generator to the end of the circuit. After that, we propagate the observable through that evolved generator. This process is repeated for each anti-noise generator in the circuit. In this implementation, each generator in a given layer is propagated to the end of the circuit in parallel. Additionally, Python multiprocessing is used to perform both the forward-propagation of the anti-noise as well as the back-propagation of the observable in parallel. This prevents a pile-up of evolved generators in memory and also maximizes compute resources.\n"
msgstr "Tulad ng tinalakay sa itaas, ginagawa ito sa dalawang hakbang. Una, ipina-propagate natin ang isang anti-noise generator patungo sa dulo ng circuit. Pagkatapos nito, ipina-propagate natin ang observable sa evolved generator na iyon. Ang prosesong ito ay inuulit para sa bawat anti-noise generator sa circuit. Sa implementasyong ito, ang bawat generator sa isang naibigay na layer ay ipina-propagate patungo sa dulo ng circuit nang parallel. Bukod dito, ginagamit ang Python multiprocessing upang isagawa nang parallel ang forward-propagation ng anti-noise pati na rin ang back-propagation ng observable. Pinipigilan nito ang pag-ipon ng evolved generators sa memory at pinapahusay din ang paggamit ng compute resources.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When running PNA, you always need to provide a noisy circuit and observable. If your noisy circuit is a boxed circuit with `InjectNoise` annotations, you need to provide the mapping we created in the step above. One can also pass a non-boxed circuit containing `PauliLindbladError` instructions from `qiskit-aer`. In that case, `refs_to_noise_models` does not have to be provided. In addition to the primary inputs, also consider the following:\n"
msgstr "Kapag pinapatakbo ang PNA, kailangan mo palaging magbigay ng isang noisy circuit at observable. Kung ang iyong noisy circuit ay isang boxed circuit na may `InjectNoise` annotations, kailangan mong ibigay ang mapping na nabuo natin sa hakbang sa itaas. Maaari ring magpasa ng isang non-boxed circuit na naglalaman ng `PauliLindbladError` instructions mula sa `qiskit-aer`. Sa kasong iyon, hindi na kailangang ibigay ang `refs_to_noise_models`. Bukod sa mga pangunahing input, isaalang-alang din ang mga sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_err_terms`: The number of terms to keep in each anti-noise generator as it is forward-propagated. Allowing this to be larger generally increases accuracy, but this behavior is not guaranteed to be monotonic.\n"
msgstr "`max_err_terms`: Ang bilang ng mga termino na papanatilihin sa bawat anti-noise generator habang ito ay forward-propagated. Ang pagpapahintulot dito na maging mas malaki ay karaniwang nagpapataas ng accuracy, ngunit hindi garantisadong monotonic ang ugaling ito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_obs_terms`: The number of terms to keep in the noise-mitigating observable, $\\tilde{O}$, as it is back-propagated through the evolved anti-noise. Larger values generally increase accuracy, but it is not guaranteed to do so monotonically.\n"
msgstr "`max_obs_terms`: Ang bilang ng mga termino na papanatilihin sa noise-mitigating observable, $\\tilde{O}$, habang ito ay back-propagated sa evolved anti-noise. Ang mas malalaking value ay karaniwang nagpapataas ng accuracy, ngunit hindi garantisadong monotonic ito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_processes`: The number of cores to dedicate to the process. Remember, the generators are forward-propagated and applied to the observable in parallel.\n"
msgstr "`num_processes`: Ang bilang ng cores na ilalaan sa proseso. Tandaan, ang mga generator ay forward-propagated at inilalapat sa observable nang parallel.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`search_step`: The back-propagation step uses a greedy method to approximately conjugate two operators in the Pauli basis. This method can be sped up by increasing `search_step`. See the [`pauli-prop` docs](https://qiskit.github.io/pauli-prop/) for more information.\n"
msgstr "`search_step`: Ginagamit ng back-propagation step ang isang greedy method upang aproksimadong i-conjugate ang dalawang operator sa Pauli basis. Ang method na ito ay maaaring pabilisin sa pamamagitan ng pagtaas ng `search_step`. Tingnan ang [`pauli-prop` docs](https://qiskit.github.io/pauli-prop/) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_to_measure`: While this variable isn't an input to `generate_noise_mitigating_observable`, we use it to control how many terms from $\\tilde{O}$ we actually want to measure. Here we only measure the top 30 terms, which are the original terms in our observable. The terms have now been re-scaled such that measuring them has the effect of mitigating the learned gate noise. Although we only measure 30 terms from $\\tilde{O}$, it is often still useful to allow it to grow large, as that increases the precision of the leading terms' scaling factors.\n"
msgstr "`num_to_measure`: Bagama't hindi ito isang input sa `generate_noise_mitigating_observable`, ginagamit natin ito upang kontrolin kung ilang termino mula sa $\\tilde{O}$ ang gusto talaga nating sukatin. Dito, sinusukat lamang natin ang top 30 terms, na siyang orihinal na mga termino sa ating observable. Ang mga termino ay na-re-scale na ngayon upang ang pagsukat sa kanila ay may epekto ng pagpapagaan sa natutunang gate noise. Bagama't 30 termino lamang mula sa $\\tilde{O}$ ang ating sinusukat, madalas na kapaki-pakinabang pa rin na hayaang lumaki ito, dahil pinapataas nito ang precision ng scaling factors ng mga leading terms.\n"

