# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transform the measurement bases to canonical form {#transform-the-measurement-bases-to-canonical-form}"
msgstr "Transform the measurement bases to canonical form {#transform-the-measurement-bases-to-canonical-form}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we find a minimal set of bases to measure such that we can fully cover every Pauli term in the measured observable (*many observables may be measured simultaneously if they commute qubit-wise*). Since we are only measuring the terms in our original observable, which is the sum of all single-`Z` Paulis, a single basis is needed: the all-`Z` basis.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, hinahanap natin ang isang minimal set ng mga basis na susukatin upang ganap nating masaklaw ang bawat Pauli term sa nasukat na observable (*maaaring sukatin nang sabay-sabay ang maraming observable kung sila ay commute qubit-wise*). Dahil sinusukat lamang natin ang mga termino sa ating orihinal na observable, na siyang kabuuan ng lahat ng single-`Z` Paulis, iisang basis lamang ang kailangan: ang all-`Z` basis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to finding a set of Pauli measurement bases, we need to map these Pauli terms to the canonical form expected by the `Executor`. For more information on canonical qubit ordering, visit the [Samplomatic docs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-ordering-convention).\n"
msgstr "Bukod sa paghahanap ng set ng Pauli measurement bases, kailangan nating i-map ang mga Pauli term na ito sa canonical form na inaasahan ng `Executor`. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa canonical qubit ordering, bisitahin ang [Samplomatic docs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-ordering-convention).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute quantum experiments {#step-3-execute-quantum-experiments}"
msgstr "Step 3: Execute quantum experiments {#step-3-execute-quantum-experiments}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify how to sample in the `QuantumProgram` {#specify-how-to-sample-in-the-quantumprogram}"
msgstr "Specify how to sample in the `QuantumProgram` {#specify-how-to-sample-in-the-quantumprogram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now set up the `QuantumProgram`, which serves as the central container for all circuits and sampling configurations that will be executed by the `Executor`. This object defines how randomized circuit instances are generated, batched, and executed to produce the measurement results used in PNA.\n"
msgstr "Itatakda na natin ngayon ang `QuantumProgram`, na siyang sentral na container para sa lahat ng circuit at sampling configuration na isasagawa ng `Executor`. Tinutukoy ng object na ito kung paano nabubuo, nagagrupo, at naisasagawa ang mga randomized circuit instance upang makabuo ng mga resulta ng measurement na ginagamit sa PNA.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `QuantumProgram` can contain multiple items, each consisting of a template circuit and a corresponding `samplex` object that defines how randomizations are applied. This abstraction allows the `Executor` to handle the entire workflow as a single, modular program &mdash; from randomized circuit generation to shot collection and aggregation.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang `QuantumProgram` ay maaaring maglaman ng maraming item, na ang bawat isa ay binubuo ng isang template circuit at kaukulang `samplex` object na tumutukoy kung paano inilalapat ang mga randomization. Ang abstraction na ito ay nagbibigay-daan sa `Executor` na hawakan ang buong workflow bilang isang solo, modular na program &mdash; mula sa randomized circuit generation hanggang sa shot collection at aggregation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this step, we create a `QuantumProgram` that runs our PNA experiment using the template circuit and `samplex` we constructed earlier. The configuration includes the following elements:\n"
msgstr "Sa hakbang na ito, gumagawa tayo ng isang `QuantumProgram` na nagpapatakbo ng ating PNA experiment gamit ang template circuit at `samplex` na binuo natin kanina. Kasama sa configuration ang mga sumusunod na elemento:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`template_circuit`: The circuit containing all the gates necessary to implement all desired randomizations (from twirling randomizations, parameters, and so on).\n"
msgstr "`template_circuit`: Ang circuit na naglalaman ng lahat ng gates na kailangan upang ipatupad ang lahat ng ninanais na randomization (mula sa twirling randomizations, parameters, at iba pa).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`samplex`: An object defining a probability distribution over all possible circuit randomizations from which to sample.\n"
msgstr "`samplex`: Isang object na tumutukoy ng probability distribution sa lahat ng posibleng circuit randomizations kung saan mag-sasample.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`samplex_arguments`: Bindings necessary to fully define the `samplex`\n"
msgstr "`samplex_arguments`: Bindings na kailangan upang ganap na matukoy ang `samplex`\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`basis_changes`: Here is where we specify a set of bases to measure that will cover all of the Pauli terms in the measured observable.\n"
msgstr "`basis_changes`: Dito natin tinutukoy ang isang set ng mga basis na susukatin na sasaklaw sa lahat ng Pauli terms sa nasukat na observable.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`noise_scales.ref`: We set each noise layer's scale to `0.0` to prevent any additional noise from being injected into our samples.\n"
msgstr "`noise_scales.ref`: Itinatakda natin ang scale ng bawat noise layer sa `0.0` upang maiwasan ang anumang karagdagang noise na ma-inject sa ating mga sample.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`pauli_lindblad_maps`: Required if `noise_scales` are passed. This just maps noise layers to the associated noise model.\n"
msgstr "`pauli_lindblad_maps`: Kinakailangan kung ipapasa ang `noise_scales`. Ito ay nag-mamap lamang ng noise layers sa kaugnay na noise model.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`shape`: A shape tuple to extend the implicit shape defined by `samplex_arguments`. Non-trivial axes introduced by this extension enumerate randomizations.\n"
msgstr "`shape`: Isang shape tuple upang palawigin ang implicit na shape na tinutukoy ng `samplex_arguments`. Ang mga non-trivial axes na ipinapakilala ng extension na ito ay nag-eenumerate ng mga randomization.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample the circuit using the `Executor` {#sample-the-circuit-using-the-executor}"
msgstr "Sample the circuit using the `Executor` {#sample-the-circuit-using-the-executor}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have defined our `QuantumProgram`, executing the experiment is straightforward. We simply instantiate the `Executor` object, provide it with the backend, and run the program.\n"
msgstr "Ngayong natukoy na natin ang ating `QuantumProgram`, simple na lamang ang pagsasagawa ng eksperimento. Iina-instantiate lamang natin ang `Executor` object, ibinibigay dito ang backend, at pinapatakbo ang program.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Reconstruct and analyze results {#step-4-reconstruct-and-analyze-results}"
msgstr "Step 4: Reconstruct and analyze results {#step-4-reconstruct-and-analyze-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To calculate an error-mitigated expectation value, we do the following:\n"
msgstr "Upang makalkula ang isang error-mitigated expectation value, ginagawa natin ang mga sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the TREX scaling factors based on the learned noise affecting the measurements,\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang TREX scaling factors batay sa natutunang noise na nakakaapekto sa mga measurement,\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate a mask for keeping only post-selected samples, and\n"
msgstr "Bumuo ng mask para sa pagpapanatili lamang ng mga post-selected sample, at\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the `executor_expectation_values` function from `qiskit-addon-utils` for combining all of the data into an error-mitigated expectation value.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang function na `executor_expectation_values` mula sa `qiskit-addon-utils` upang pagsamahin ang lahat ng data patungo sa isang error-mitigated expectation value.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare mitigation strategies: PNA, PNA+TREX, PNA+PS, PNA+PS+TREX {#compare-mitigation-strategies-pna-pnatrex-pnaps-pnapstrex}"
msgstr "Compare mitigation strategies: PNA, PNA+TREX, PNA+PS, PNA+PS+TREX {#compare-mitigation-strategies-pna-pnatrex-pnaps-pnapstrex}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We compute and visualize expectation values for several mitigation variants using the `Executor` results.\n"
msgstr "Kinakalkula at ina-visualize natin ang mga expectation value para sa ilang mitigation variant gamit ang mga resulta ng `Executor`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/extracted-outputs/8df9366c-d456-416b-80ab-3b941a07a935-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/propagated-noise-absorption/extracted-outputs/8df9366c-d456-416b-80ab-3b941a07a935-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The results demonstrate the cumulative benefits of combining different error-mitigation techniques. The plain PNA approach already restores the expectation value close to the ideal benchmark, indicating that propagating inverse noise channels into the observable effectively compensates for two-qubit gate errors.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng mga resulta ang cumulative na benepisyo ng pagsasama-sama ng iba't ibang error-mitigation technique. Ang plain PNA approach ay naibabalik na ang expectation value nang malapit sa ideal benchmark, na nagpapahiwatig na ang pag-propagate ng inverse noise channels sa observable ay epektibong nagbabayad-pinsala sa two-qubit gate errors.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding TREX reweighting (PNA+TREX) slightly improves the estimate by correcting for sampling imbalance in the randomized circuits.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagdaragdag ng TREX reweighting (PNA+TREX) ay bahagyang nagpapahusay sa estimate sa pamamagitan ng pagwawasto sa sampling imbalance sa mga randomized circuit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-selection (PNA+PS) provides a more noticeable boost by filtering out inconsistent measurement outcomes that likely result from residual errors.\n"
msgstr "Ang post-selection (PNA+PS) ay nagbibigay ng mas kapansin-pansing pagbuti sa pamamagitan ng pag-filter sa mga hindi pare-parehong measurement outcome na malamang na dulot ng mga natitirang error.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, combining both (PNA+PS+TREX) yields the most accurate result, nearly matching the ideal value, showing how these mitigation strategies reinforce each other.\n"
msgstr "Sa huli, ang pagsasama ng dalawa (PNA+PS+TREX) ay nagbibigay ng pinaka-tumpak na resulta, halos katumbas ng ideal value, na nagpapakita kung paano pinagtitibay ng mga mitigation strategy na ito ang isa't isa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overall, the comparison highlights that PNA serves as a robust foundation for noise-aware expectation value estimation, while TREX and post-selection offer complementary refinements for further accuracy gains.\n"
msgstr "Sa kabuuan, itinatampok ng paghahambing na ito na ang PNA ay nagsisilbing matibay na pundasyon para sa noise-aware na expectation value estimation, habang ang TREX at post-selection ay nag-aalok ng magkakaugnay na mga pagpapahusay para sa karagdagang katumpakan.\n"

